{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadratic_action_term_below_one_fifteenth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadratic_action_term_below_one_fifteenth","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.lean#L81-L86","doc":"Equivalent ratio statement: the (larger) quadratic-action term is below one\nfifteenth of the deuteron binding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadratic_action_form_a_seventy_times_too_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadratic_action_form_a_seventy_times_too_small","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.lean#L75-L79","doc":"The smaller form (A) is more than seventy times too small. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadratic_action_term_too_small_for_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadratic_action_term_too_small_for_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**Refutation (narrow).** Even *fifteen times* the larger forced-weighted\nq-Bessel quadratic-action term falls short of the deuteron binding: the term is\nat least 15× too small to *be* the binding. This kills the quadratic-action\nfunctional under the forced `y_λ` measure; the kernel and the log-free-energy\nfunctional are untouched (see file header).\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] qbessel-reeb-yweighted-gap (forced `y_λ` deflation, 2026-06-20). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadraticActionTermFormA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadraticActionTermFormA","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.lean#L61-L62","doc":"Form (A) magnitude, `|Σ_λ y_λ ΔG| = 0.056` m_e-units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadraticActionTermMe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.quadraticActionTermMe","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.lean#L56-L59","doc":"Magnitude of the forced-`y_λ`-weighted q-Bessel quadratic-action term, larger\nof the two forms tested, `|Σ_λ y_λ χ_λ ΔG| = 0.244` m_e-units (form (B) of the\ndeflation witness).  Form (A) `|Σ_λ y_λ ΔG| = 0.056` is smaller still. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.deuteronTargetMe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.deuteronTargetMe","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselQuadraticActionTerm.lean#L51-L54","doc":"Deuteron binding in electron-mass units, `B(D)/m_e` (the target any candidate\nbinding term must reproduce).  ≈ 4.353  (`target_signed` magnitude,\n`2026-05-18-delta-lambda-gating-context.md`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}